    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "BODY",
      "narration_text": "A chatbot responds once per message. You type, it answers, and then it waits for you. You're the loop. If it gives you code, you run it, paste the error back, and ask again. An agent runs its own loop. It decides the next step, uses a tool, checks the result, and keeps going until the goal is met. Think of a chatbot as a calculator, and an agent as an intern with a to-do list.",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "speed": 0.95,
      "estimated_duration_s": 23.0,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
